class:: ScannedNetworkOsc
summary:: Scan a moving mass-spring network as an oscillator waveform
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

ScannedNetworkOsc separates a slow one-dimensional mass-spring simulation from
an audio-rate scanner. The network supplies a changing wavetable while the
signed scan frequency supplies pitch. This original implementation follows the
scanned-synthesis model described by Smaragdis and uses a bounded
velocity-Verlet integration with a conservative, automatically substepped
physical timestep.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Osc::. Both scan a stored shape, but
Osc reads a Buffer while ScannedNetworkOsc continuously evolves private
displacement and velocity arrays.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed scan frequency in hertz.

argument:: rate
Physical evolution speed, clamped to code::0..20::. Zero freezes displacement
and velocity exactly while scanning continues.

argument:: stiffness
Neighbor coupling, clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: centering
Restoring force toward zero, clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: damping
Velocity loss, clamped to code::0..2::.

argument:: excite
Continuous force near code::position::, clamped to code::-8..8::.

argument:: strike
A nonpositive-to-positive edge applies one spatially smoothed impulse.

argument:: strikeAmp
Signed impulse amplitude, clamped to code::-8..8::.

argument:: position
Normalized excitation location, clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: scanPath
Initialization-rate path: code::0:: forward, code::1:: alternating direction,
or code::2:: folded.

argument:: nodes
Initialization-rate node count from code::16:: through code::512::. CPU and
private state grow approximately linearly with this value.

argument:: topology
Initialization-rate topology: code::0:: fixed endpoints or code::1:: circular.

argument:: initShape
Initialization-rate displacement: code::0:: sine, code::1:: triangle,
code::2:: seeded smooth noise, or code::3:: silence.

argument:: seed
Initialization-rate nonnegative deterministic seed.

argument:: mul
Output multiplier applied to both channels.

argument:: add
Offset added to both channels after multiplication.

returns::
An array containing the scanned signal followed by smoothed normalized network
energy.

method:: kr

ScannedNetworkOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

Physical updates run on a fixed 1 kHz scheduler and are independent of the
audio scanner. A strike received while code::rate:: is zero is ignored so the
documented freeze is exact. Fixed topology keeps both endpoints at zero.
Network state is allocated only during UGen construction.

examples::

code::
(
{ ScannedNetworkOsc.ar(90, rate: 0.15)[0] * 0.08 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    var hit = Dust.kr(0.8);
    var scan = ScannedNetworkOsc.ar(
        62, rate: 0.3, stiffness: 0.45,
        damping: 0.015, strike: hit, strikeAmp: 0.5,
        position: LFNoise1.kr(0.2).range(0, 1),
        nodes: 192
    );
    Pan2.ar(scan[0], scan[1].linlin(0, 1, -0.7, 0.7)) * 0.07;
}.play;
)
::

